B.a0s=new A.du("How do I get my team on FolioMed?","On the Wards tab, tap Set Up a Ward, name it and choose its type (PNC, NICU, PICU, paediatric, adult or other \u2014 it sets the checks behind the status dots). You get a 5-digit code \u2014 tap Invite to share it. Colleagues tap Join a Ward and type it in.")
B.a09=new A.du("What do the four tabs do?","Today shows Up Next \u2014 overdue reminders, urgent notes and your jobs, most pressing first \u2014 then counts that open the full lists, and the latest notes. Patients lists everyone on your wards. Wards is where you create, join and manage wards and units. Profile holds your details and settings.")
B.a0m=new A.du("Doctor or nurse \u2014 what changes?","Both see the same patients and notes. Doctors post notes from the compose button; nurses confirm notes through the confirm sheet, which records what was done. You can switch role in Profile.")
B.ajE=s([B.a0s,B.a09,B.a0m],t.wX)
B.a_Y=new A.jY("Getting started",B.ajE)
B.a0l=new A.du("How do I admit a patient?","Tap the person+ button on Today or Patients. Name is the only required field; choose the ward (and unit, if your ward uses them). FolioMed gives every patient a permanent ID such as FM000123.")
B.a0t=new A.du("How do I edit, transfer or discharge?","Open the patient and tap \u2022\u2022\u2022 in the top corner. Edit details changes the record; Transfer moves the patient \u2014 with their notes and reminders \u2014 to another ward you belong to; Discharge moves them to the Discharged list, and Readmit brings them back under the same ID.")
B.a_Z=new A.du("What do the coloured dots mean?","Each admitted patient has a dot beside the bed number. Red (filled) needs action now, amber (filled with a ring) means watch, green (ring) is settled, and grey (thin ring) means no status has been set on a PICU, paediatric or adult ward. The most serious reason wins: a status staff set by hand (Stable, Watch or Sick), urgent notes waiting to be confirmed, overdue reminders and urgent or overdue jobs, and checks that depend on the ward type. On PNC and NICU those are the latest bilirubin against the guideline line (red when it is above the line and phototherapy isn\u2019t running), weight loss from birth (amber beyond 7%, red at 10%), a missing gestational age or risk factors, and on NICU a birth weight not regained by day 14. On PICU, ticking Ventilated or Inotropes while the status says Stable turns it amber. Wards of type Other use the newborn checks for babies under 28 days. Open the patient to see every reason. The dots are a prompt to look, never a diagnosis.")
B.a0g=new A.du("How do observations and NEWS2 / PEWS work?","For patients 28 days and older, the patient page has an Observations section. Tap Add Observations and enter what you measured \u2014 the score updates as you type. Patients 16 and over get NEWS2 (not for use in pregnancy); children get Brighton PEWS, where you score behaviour, cardiovascular and respiratory 0\u20133 from the descriptions using your chart\u2019s normal ranges for age. On paediatric, adult and Other wards the latest observations colour the status dot for 12 hours: NEWS2 5 or more, or PEWS 4 or more or any part scoring 3, is red; a single NEWS2 parameter scoring 3, or PEWS 3, is amber. A set with missing values can still raise the colour. The scoring has not yet been checked by a clinician for your unit \u2014 confirm against your chart.")
B.a0c=new A.du("How does the shift handover work?","FolioMed uses I-PASS. On each patient\u2019s page, keep a short Handover summary (what\u2019s going on and the plan) and add If / Then lines for what the next shift should do if something changes. At shift change, open Patients \u2192 Census & handover \u2192 Handover and tap Start Handover. Each card shows the status dot and its reasons (Illness severity), the summary (Patient summary), open jobs and reminders (Action list) and the If / Then lines (Situation awareness). The person taking over sees \u201cHandover from \u2026\u201d on Today, opens it on their own phone and taps Received on each patient \u2014 or Question to receive with a question. Finish Handover records anyone not received as missed. Share sends the same list as text.")
B.a01=new A.du("How do I set a patient\u2019s status?","Open the patient and tap Status at the top of Overview. Choose Stable, Watch or Sick, add a short reason if it helps, and (on PICU) tick the support in place. Saving the same status again counts as a review; a status not reviewed in 12 hours on PICU, or 24 hours elsewhere, shows faded with Review. A status can raise the colour but can\u2019t hide an automatic red \u2014 that clears when its cause does. Every change is written on the timeline. The ward owner sets the ward type on the ward\u2019s page (Wards \u2192 the ward \u2192 About).")
B.a0o=new A.du("What is My Patients?","Tap the star on a patient\u2019s page to follow them. The My Patients filter on the Patients tab shows everyone you follow, plus patients you\u2019ve written a note about in the last 48 hours or have an open job for. Follows are private to you, and end when the patient is discharged or moves to a ward you\u2019re not in.")
B.a0a=new A.du("How do consultants and tags work?","On a patient\u2019s page, under Team, set the consultant (names already used in the ward are offered) and tick clinical tags such as NPO or Isolation. Tags show as small chips on the Patients list, and Filter (next to the sort button) narrows the list to one consultant or one tag. The ward owner edits the ward\u2019s tag list on the ward\u2019s page. Search also finds consultant names and tags.")
B.a08=new A.du("How do clinical photos work?","On a patient\u2019s page, under Photos, tap Add Photo, then take or choose one. FolioMed shrinks it before upload (usually from a few MB to about 200\u2013300 KB, or larger with High detail for X-rays) and removes hidden data such as location. Add a caption, tick Consent obtained, and Upload. Photos are stored online in FolioMed \u2014 never in your phone\u2019s gallery \u2014 and only members of the patient\u2019s current ward can see them; they move with the patient on transfer. Each photo adds a line to the timeline. On Android, screenshots are blocked while photos are on screen; iPhone and web can\u2019t block them, so treat photos as part of the patient\u2019s record.")
B.a0p=new A.du("What is the Workload report?","For the ward owner and admins: Wards \u2192 the ward \u2192 Workload (admins: the ward\u2019s page in Admin). For the last 24 hours, 7 or 30 days it shows jobs added and done (and the typical time to done), how quickly urgent notes were confirmed, reminders done late, handovers and missed patients \u2014 overall and per shift \u2014 plus counts per person, listed A\u2013Z for planning rather than ranking. The owner sets the shift start times on the ward\u2019s page (default 08:00, 14:00 and 20:00).")
B.a00=new A.du("Can I find a baby by the mother\u2019s name?","Yes. Search on the Patients tab matches the patient\u2019s name, the mother\u2019s name, bed, diagnosis, FolioMed ID and hospital ID.")
B.ahZ=s([B.a0l,B.a0t,B.a_Z,B.a0g,B.a0c,B.a01,B.a0o,B.a0a,B.a08,B.a0p,B.a00],t.wX)
B.a_R=new A.jY("Patients",B.ahZ)
B.a0b=new A.du("How are hours of life worked out?","From the birth date and time entered on the patient. Age shows in hours for the first week, then days, months and years.")
B.a06=new A.du(u.x,"When you add a birth time, FolioMed asks whether you\u2019ll send the investigations at 48 or 72 hours and how early to remind you (8 or 12 hours). At the hour it asks the ward whether they were sent, then asks for the results.")
B.a0_=new A.du("What do the bilirubin lines mean?","The chart plots each reading against the phototherapy and exchange lines for the baby\u2019s gestation (and, for AAP, neurotoxicity risk factors). The guideline follows the gestational age: NICE below 35 weeks, AAP 2022 from 35 weeks (record the neurotoxicity risk factors \u2014 on the baby\u2019s page or while entering results \u2014 for AAP lines). This is decision support only \u2014 always confirm against the guideline and your clinical judgement.")
B.a04=new A.du("What is the discharge checklist?","On a newborn\u2019s page, Discharge Checklist shows what\u2019s done and what isn\u2019t. FolioMed fills in the investigations, TSH, blood grouping, OAE, a bilirubin and a weight from the last 24 hours, and whether phototherapy has stopped. Staff tick Vitamin K, BCG, OPV-0, Hepatitis B, feeding, urine and meconium, counselling and follow-up. If anything is open when you discharge, FolioMed lists it first; you can still discharge.")
B.a0w=new A.du("Why does AAP ask about risk factors?",'AAP 2022 uses lower thresholds when a baby has a neurotoxicity risk factor such as haemolysis, G6PD deficiency or sepsis. Record them (or "none") under Bilirubin on the patient page; until then FolioMed won\u2019t apply AAP lines.')
B.a5t=s([B.a0b,B.a06,B.a0_,B.a04,B.a0w],t.wX)
B.a_Q=new A.jY("Newborns",B.a5t)
B.a0f=new A.du("What\u2019s in the Tools tab?","Bedside calculators \u2014 emergency drugs for NICU and PICU, infusion rates with standard syringes, fluids and GIR (with dextrose mixing), corrected age, exchange transfusion volumes, UVC/UAC and ETT \u2014 low blood glucose, electrolytes and anion gap, blood pressure centiles, the national vaccine schedule \u2014 and newborn scores: Apgar, Downes, Silverman-Anderson, Thompson, LATCH, New Ballard and Modified Sarnat. A finished score can be copied or added to the baby\u2019s notes. Tap Fill from a Baby to fill in weight, day of life and gestation from an admitted patient, then check each value.")
B.a0k=new A.du("How do Emergency Drugs and infusions work?","Enter the weight and choose NICU or PICU. One-off doses show the dose, the volume to draw up and how to dilute it; infusions show the standard syringe (1 mL/h gives a set dose) with strengths from \xbd\xd7 to 4\xd7, syringe sizes and a rate table. From a baby\u2019s page or the Infusion Rate tool you can start an infusion on the record; changes and stops go on the timeline and into handover.")
B.a0r=new A.du("Who signs off a drug?","Each ward keeps its own drug list (ward page \u2192 Drug List). The owner can set the ward\u2019s vial strengths, standard syringes and notes, or hide a drug; any doctor of the ward can sign a drug off after comparing it with the unit\u2019s reference. A sign-off covers exactly what was shown \u2014 if the doses, vial or syringe change, the drug shows \u201cChanged \u2014 recheck\u201d.")
B.a05=new A.du("Can I rely on the numbers?","Each tool shows its formula and source. Until your unit has checked them, every tool says so at the top \u2014 confirm against your own protocol, and have a second person check drug rates.")
B.aeL=s([B.a0f,B.a0k,B.a0r,B.a05],t.wX)
B.a_W=new A.jY("Tools",B.aeL)
B.a07=new A.du("What is the job list?","The day\u2019s tasks for each patient, such as \u201cRepeat TSB\u201d or \u201cPaeds review\u201d, shared by the whole ward. Add one from Today (+ \u2192 New Job) or from the patient\u2019s page. Tap the circle to tick it off; FolioMed records who did it and when.")
B.a0n=new A.du("How do I give a job to someone?","When adding a job, set For to a colleague on the ward and they get a notification. Leave it as Anyone for whoever is free. On any job, tap it and choose I\u2019ll Do It or Assign To\u2026.")
B.a0d=new A.du("Where do finished and old jobs go?","Ticked jobs stay under Jobs \u2192 Done until midnight and on the patient\u2019s page for 24 hours. Jobs move with the patient on transfer and drop off the list once the patient is discharged.")
B.aiF=s([B.a07,B.a0n,B.a0d],t.wX)
B.a_T=new A.jY("Jobs",B.aiF)
B.a03=new A.du("Who sees a note?","Everyone in that patient\u2019s ward, in real time. Urgent notes are highlighted and alert the team.")
B.a0v=new A.du("Where are all the notes?","On Today, tap Show All next to Latest Notes (or Notes to Confirm). The \u21d5 button there switches between one line per note and full notes.")
B.a02=new A.du("How do reminders follow up?",'When a reminder is due, FolioMed asks "has this been done?". Yes closes it for the whole ward; Not yet asks again in an hour.')
B.ab6=s([B.a03,B.a0v,B.a02],t.wX)
B.a_X=new A.jY("Notes and reminders",B.ab6)
B.a0i=new A.du("What is a unit?","A team inside a ward, such as Unit A and Unit B. The ward owner creates units on the ward page; patients can then be assigned to one. Everyone in the ward still sees every unit.")
B.a0h=new A.du("How do I see only my unit?","Open the ward and set My unit. Today and Patients then open on your unit; use the filter button to change it.")
B.a0e=new A.du("Census and handover","On Patients, tap the clipboard button. Census gives the day\u2019s head count; Handover lists each baby with what needs attention, ready to share.")
B.ac6=s([B.a0i,B.a0h,B.a0e],t.wX)
B.a_U=new A.jY("Wards and units",B.ac6)
B.a0u=new A.du("I\u2019m not getting alerts","On Android, open Profile \u2192 Alert Setup and make sure every item shows a tick. Some brands also need auto-start allowed \u2014 the screen tells you where.")
B.ag4=s([B.a0u],t.wX)
B.a_S=new A.jY("Alerts",B.ag4)
B.a0q=new A.du("Where is patient data kept?","In FolioMed\u2019s secure database, visible only to members of the patient\u2019s ward. Photos you scan are read on your phone and never uploaded. See the privacy policy for details.")
B.a0j=new A.du("How do I delete my account?","Profile \u2192 Delete account. This also deletes any wards you own, with their patients and notes, so hand ownership on first if your team still needs them.")
B.aiB=s([B.a0q,B.a0j],t.wX)
B.a_V=new A.jY("Account and privacy",B.aiB)
